 that I would need to teach that little man.

68
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:13,060
 I knew that I would need to show him

69
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:15,640
 what it meant to look a man in the eye

70
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:16,560
 whenever you shake his hand,

71
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:19,040
 how to play with passion or don't play at all,

72
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:21,320
 to never enter the pool by the stairs,

73
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:25,400
 that he shouldn't grow a wishbone where he needs a backbone,

74
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:28,320
 that he should lead by example and not by explanation,

75
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,640
 that he should always return a borrowed car

76
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:31,600
 with a full tank of gas,

77
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:34,920
 and he should never, never turn down a breath mint.

78
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:36,440
 Neither should you, gentlemen, by the way.

79
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,240
 It will serve us all.

80
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:40,200
 I know what a young man needs.

81
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,160
 I knew whenever we had a little boy

82
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,540
 exactly what I could give him.

83
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:47,040
 But then we found out we were having a little girl

84
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:50,380
 and the entire script changed for me.

85
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:52,200
 I realized in that moment

86
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:54,960
 what most normal fathers realize.

87
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,280
 I have really good reason to panic

88
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:59,440
 and I have really good reason to research,

89
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:03,840
 which is exactly what I've done over the last several months

90
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:06,080
 in anticipation of her arrival.

91
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:09,920
 I have read books on the unique challenges that women face.

92
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:11,160
 And let me just say,

93
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:13,420
 I am terrified at the thought of being a woman.

94
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:15,560
 Like it seems so much harder

95
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,480
 than what is happening for us fellas.

96
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:19,740
 I have entered into the femisphere.

97
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:21,760
 God forbid, I have listened to snippets

98
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:24,720
 of "Call Her Daddy," "The Toast,"

99
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:28,340
 and "We Can Do Hard Things" all in the name of research.

100
00:03:28,340 --> 00:03:33,160
 I have read the "Summer I Turned Pretty" subreddit

101
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:37,760
 trying to understand what grown women

102
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:41,640
 have such a fascination with a teenage love triangle for.

103
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,520
 It makes no sense to me in the slightest.

104
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:46,380
 And I have even dared try to help my wife

105
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:48,300
 pick out her wardrobe for work

106
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:51,840
 as she is going in to the office during the week.

107
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,120
 I have sat there and I have tried

108
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,720
 to kind of pick it out with her.

109
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:57,160
 And what I've realized is I do not have an eye

110
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,320
 for the boss girl life.

111
00:03:58,320 --> 00:04:00,460
 I don't know anything about fashion,

112
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:01,920
 if you can't tell already.

113
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:04,560
 I don't know that where most clothes

114
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:06,280
 apparently seem the same to me,

115
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,640
 they're so very different in her mind instead.

116
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:09,860
 After all of my research,

117
00:04:09,860 --> 00:04:11,960
 I have come to the humbling conclusion

118
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:15,560
 that I have still no idea what it takes to make a woman.

119
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:20,560
 But here's also a conclusion adjacent to that one.

120
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,320
 I don't think the world does either.

121
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:29,320
 Because as you look across the landscape of society,

122
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:31,740
 as you study what's happening on the internet,

123
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:34,200
 you realize that there is a smattering

124
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:36,320
 of different suggestions for you.

125
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:40,120
 Everyone's selling you the same idea

126
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:42,720
 just wrapped in a different kind of packaging.

127
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,960
 Some are telling you that you gotta have

128
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:46,280
 a full-time content strategy.

129
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:48,720
 You gotta have a "That Girl" morning routine,

130
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:49,800
 a hot take about something.

131
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:52,560
 You gotta have an opinion about matcha.

132
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:55,160
 To others, it's saying you need to have a hinge profile

133
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,000
 that's funny, but it's not trying too hard.

134
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,040
 You need to have a LinkedIn that screams thriving.

135
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,760
 And you have to have a Pinterest board for a wedding

136
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:02,760
 that you're not currently planning

137
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,560
 for a man that you haven't even met.

138
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:07,840
 And to others, and this is especially

139
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:09,680
 for those that have grown up in the church,

140
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:11,660
 you have a purity checklist.

141
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:13,560
 Because apparently that's a prerequisite

142
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:15,120
 in order for you to find Mr. Right.

143
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,280
 Somewhere along the way,

144
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,920
 so many of you picked up this quiet belief

145
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:21,320
 that womanhood is something you need to achieve.

146
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:25,440
 That there's a version of you who has finally arrived,

147
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:28,500
 that's finally made it, that's finally here.

148
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,240
 And yet the truth of the matter is she's never here.

149
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:32,480
 She's always just a little further down the line

150
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:33,840
 than where you are right now.

151
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:37,800
 Maybe it's a body that you need to change.

152
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:39,520
 It's a degree that's finally on the wall.

153
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:42,480
 It's an apartment that's finally furnished.

154
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,480
 Maybe it's not that.

155
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:45,880
 Maybe it's someone that finally chooses you,

156
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:47,560
 a guy that swipes right, that texts you back,

157
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:48,640
 that gets down on one knee.

158
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,920
 Maybe that girl that you know you need to be

159
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:55,260
 is the one where you have a side hustle no longer,

160
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:57,220
 but it's actually your sustainable source of income.

161
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:58,060
 I don't know what it is for you.

162
00:05:58,060 --> 00:05:58,920
 I don't know if it's professional.

163
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,040
 I don't know if it's relational.

164
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:02,040
 I don't know if it's societal.

165
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,800
 I don't know what the pressure it is that you face,

166
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:07,120
 but all of these pressures are trying to communicate to you

167
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:10,600
 that you're a failure,

168
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,600
 that you're not yet a real woman

169
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,840
 because this is what real women look like.

170
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,040
 And yet I'm here to tell you

171
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:18,680
 that you are not a failure.

172
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:20,280
 Instead, you've been sold a lie

173
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:24,540
 because womanhood is not a life goal to achieve.

174
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:27,440
 It's a gift from God to receive.

175
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:30,960
 And I need you to know that, ladies,

176
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:35,160
 that womanhood, it's not a life goal you achieve.

177
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,160
 It's a gift from God that you receive

178
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:38,460
 because that's what we see

179
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:42,480
 whenever we darken the door of Proverbs 31.

180
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:46,160
 And we get introduced to a woman that has received

181
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:48,240
 the gift of God.

182
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,820
 And as she has walked with him,

183
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:52,960
 not by way of exercising her own strength,

184
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:54,920
 but by way of depending on his,

185
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:58,000
 she becomes everything that he always intended

186
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,100
 for her to be.

187
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,240
 That's why we're gonna look

188
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,680
 at that passage of scripture tonight.

189
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:05,600
 We're in Proverbs 31, if you have a Bible.

190
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,000
 While you're doing that, here's the thing.

191
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,040
 I know so many of you,

192
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,800
 you may have a less than positive relationship

193
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:12,000
 with this passage because the Proverbs 31

194
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:16,760
 has made you feel more behind than inspired in times past.

195
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:17,600
 I get it.

196
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:21,000
 I've been studying this thing intensively,

197
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,800
 and we're gonna look at it together intensively.

198
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,720
 And as we do so, it's gonna feel like

199
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,480
 there are 27 different principles

200
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:29,000
 that you need to apply to your life

201
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,880
 in order to be everything that God has made you to be.

202
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:32,680
 That's not the truth, though.

203
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,960
 Even though you may feel like you need to wake up

204
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:36,960
 at 5 a.m. and you gotta make your own clothes,

205
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:37,920
 you gotta start baking your own bread,

206
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,360
 you gotta plant a vineyard, buy some real estate,

207
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:41,000
 feed the poor, become a successful entrepreneur,

208
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,200
 and somehow still have time for a husband and kids,

209
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:45,560
 that's not what it's saying.

210
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,960
 It's gonna feel that way,

211
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:50,440
 but that's not actually what it's communicating.

212
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:52,400
 Which is funny, even as I say that,

213
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:55,600
 bake your own bread, make your own clothes,

214
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,100
 plant your own vineyard.

215
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:58,440
 Some of you are in your grandma era,

216
00:07:58,440 --> 00:07:59,880
 and that's like kind of the thing that you're into.

217
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:01,840
 You're like, man, I'm working on this right now, you know?

218
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,720
 I do actually wanna be that kind of woman.

219
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:05,440
 I do wanna be a sourdough baddie.

220
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,680
 I do want to knit something together.

221
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:11,720
 I absolutely want to be a plant girly.

222
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,080
 You can do that on your own time.

223
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:14,600
 That's not what this passage of scripture

224
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:17,260
 is actually trying to teach you to do.

225
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,360
 It's trying to teach you something different.

226
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,360
 What this passage is trying to tell you

227
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:21,800
 is that the point is not

228
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,680
 that you should imitate her every action.

229
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:26,360
 Instead, you should imitate the wisdom

230
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:28,720
 that undergirds her every action,

231
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:31,520
 because here's what happens over the course of Proverbs.

232
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:33,200
 Whenever you open up its pages,

233
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:36,520
 you learn that it is a father speaking to a son

234
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,960
 about what should be true of him.

235
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:40,520
 And as the father teaches to his son from Proverbs 1

236
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,240
 all the way here to the very end,

237
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:46,440
 he is unpacking the wisdom of lady wisdom,

238
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:50,000
 that she is personified as this guide

239
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,680
 that is teaching him how to walk and how to go.

240
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:55,080
 And yet, as you get to the very end of Proverbs,

241
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:57,160
 you arrive at chapter 31,

242
00:08:57,160 --> 00:09:00,640
 where lady wisdom is no longer just a concept.

243
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:02,860
 She has actually been embodied,

244
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:05,400
 personified as a woman herself,

245
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:09,160
 because it's written by King Limwell's mother.

246
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:12,200
 And what we know is that King Limwell's mother

247
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,480
 is looking at him and is saying,

248
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:15,320
 "Hey, you don't yet have a wife,

249
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:18,220
 "but here's the type of woman you should seek.

250
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:19,060
 "This is what it looks like.

251
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:20,300
 "If you find an excellent wife,

252
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:22,580
 "you must find an excellent woman."

253
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:25,920
 And so we're gonna look at it.

254
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:26,960
 It's amazing.

255
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:30,680
 The entire Proverb, it's written as a 22-verse acrostic.

256
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:33,520
 What that means is every single verse

257
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:37,240
 starts with a letter of the Hebrew alphabet,

258
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:38,440
 and it goes from A to Z.

259
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:41,560
 It moves sequentially across the way.

260
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:43,920
 We won't look at it like that for the sake of our time,

261
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:47,320
 but the reason why it does it is it wants you to know

262
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:49,920
 from A to Z what wisdom looks like

263
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:52,800
 in the life of a godly woman.

264
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,640
 And it's also written like this,

