00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:42,640
 and the week before and the week before that,

526
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:45,720
 it all actually generally applies to humanity.

527
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:47,160
 We're just trying to show who has,

528
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,600
 where it's more oriented towards

529
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,520
 according to the specific gender.

530
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:51,880
 But this pertains to everyone.

531
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:54,320
 Everyone is called to be trustworthy.

532
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:56,680
 So why then is Proverbs 31 making it a big deal

533
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:57,580
 in this moment?

534
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:01,000
 Why is this applied to women within this context,

535
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,020
 within the context of becoming a wife?

536
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:05,240
 I'll tell you.

537
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:09,240
 Because no one can make a man

538
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:11,900
 feel more vulnerable than a woman.

539
00:21:11,900 --> 00:21:14,400
 No one.

540
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:16,100
 No one can do it.

541
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:18,040
 His boss can't do it, his friends can't do it,

542
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:20,080
 his parents can't do it, his heroes can't do it,

543
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:20,960
 his team can't do it.

544
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:22,520
 Doesn't matter how bad they're playing,

545
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:25,920
 they cannot make him feel more vulnerable than you can.

546
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:28,300
 And the reason why is because you get access

547
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:32,580
 to parts of who he is that no one else gets access to.

548
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:37,760
 Like you get to see the secrets of his soul.

549
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:41,060
 You get to listen to the pain of his experience.

550
00:21:41,060 --> 00:21:44,720
 You get to actually process with those dormant emotions

551
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:46,720
 he very seldomly lets out

552
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:49,040
 and doesn't actually know how to process through.

553
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:51,260
 You get access to parts of him

554
00:21:51,260 --> 00:21:52,800
 that the world does not get access to

555
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:54,000
 because that's what love does.

556
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,640
 Love begets vulnerability.

557
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,720
 And as love is instigated between the two of you,

558
00:21:58,720 --> 00:22:00,440
 he will open himself up

559
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:04,120
 and you will have the opportunity to see more of who he is,

560
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:06,380
 that he's not all rough and tumble,

561
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:09,460
 that he's not strong and stern and stalwart.

562
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:11,940
 You're gonna see he's actually a little bit softer

563
00:22:11,940 --> 00:22:14,140
 than you think on the inside.

564
00:22:14,140 --> 00:22:15,540
 And because you see that,

565
00:22:15,540 --> 00:22:20,560
 it's going to make him so very vulnerable.

566
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:24,640
 And in that moment,

567
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:26,040
 you will have the power

568
00:22:26,040 --> 00:22:29,240
 to make him feel like a hero or a zero.

569
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:33,100
 That power lies in your hands.

570
00:22:33,100 --> 00:22:35,040
 That is why it is imperative

571
00:22:35,040 --> 00:22:37,680
 that you, a godly woman,

572
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:40,220
 know how to present yourself as trustworthy.

573
00:22:40,220 --> 00:22:45,120
 I get critiques and comments all the time

574
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:47,560
 from people about what I do up here.

575
00:22:47,560 --> 00:22:50,960
 And I listen to 'em and I learn from 'em,

576
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:52,740
 but I don't linger with 'em.

577
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:54,600
 Because at the end of the day,

578
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:56,680
 they're helpful to a certain degree,

579
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:59,120
 but they do not deserve to rob me of my sleep.

580
00:22:59,120 --> 00:23:02,280
 But my wife, my wife made one comment

581
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:04,280
 about something I said that wasn't helpful

582
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:06,840
 or felt a little inaccurate or maybe insensitive,

583
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:09,000
 and that will eat me alive.

584
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,080
 Like, it will chew me up.

585
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:14,800
 I remember conversations with her from years ago,

586
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:17,600
 like decades in the past from when we first met,

587
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:20,560
 because I cared about the things she was saying

588
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:22,880
 and she was speaking into my very identity.

589
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:25,240
 She knew the heart of who I was.

590
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:28,920
 Praise God she's trustworthy,

591
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:30,600
 because I feel safe with her.

592
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:31,960
 I feel known by her.

593
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:33,280
 I feel loved by her.

594
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:36,380
 You be trustworthy so a man can say the same about you.

595
00:23:36,380 --> 00:23:40,480
 You need to know how you do with what he offers

596
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:44,360
 determines just how trustworthy you really are.

597
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:46,240
 That's the first thing.

598
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:48,040
 And I guess, nah, I don't have time.

599
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:48,880
 Let's keep going.

600
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:51,080
 (congregation laughing)

601
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:52,440
 Second thing you gotta know is a godly woman

602
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:54,160
 is a difference maker.

603
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:57,000
 A godly woman is a difference maker.

604
00:23:57,000 --> 00:24:02,000
 Proverbs 31, 13 says, "She seeks wool and flax.

605
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:03,560
 "She works with willing hands."

606
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:04,440
 I love this.

607
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:07,560
 This woman, she sees potential in the world

608
00:24:07,560 --> 00:24:09,560
 and she actualizes it.

609
00:24:09,560 --> 00:24:11,840
 Like, she seeks out wool and flax,

610
00:24:11,840 --> 00:24:12,680
 butter, wool, and flax.

611
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:17,680
 She sees wool for the winter, flax for the summer,

612
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:21,240
 and she works hard at developing those raw materials

613
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:23,520
 into the finished goods that will bless not only her,

614
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:25,820
 but her family and the surrounding community.

615
00:24:25,820 --> 00:24:26,920
 That's who she is.

616
00:24:26,920 --> 00:24:27,760
 And it's amazing.

617
00:24:27,760 --> 00:24:28,640
 It's both wool and flax.

618
00:24:28,640 --> 00:24:30,600
 It's not just a seasonal sort of hard work.

619
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:32,180
 It's an all the time kind of hard work.

620
00:24:32,180 --> 00:24:33,920
 That's who she is.

621
00:24:33,920 --> 00:24:37,400
 We see that she is a difference maker,

622
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:39,520
 and she's this way in four different ways,

623
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:40,900
 if you're kind of taking notes.

624
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:42,600
 Main bullet is she's a difference maker,

625
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:44,640
 but there's four sub-bullets to this.

626
00:24:44,640 --> 00:24:46,800
 The first way that this actually works itself out

627
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:48,600
 is she's resourceful.

628
00:24:48,600 --> 00:24:49,680
 She's resourceful.

629
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:54,040
 Like, she knows what needs to get done,

630
00:24:54,040 --> 00:24:56,120
 and she isn't afraid to get it done.

631
00:24:56,120 --> 00:25:00,360
 Like, my wife, as of today, she's eight months pregnant.

632
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:02,320
 It's gonna be awesome looking back on this years from now

633
00:25:02,320 --> 00:25:04,200
 and realizing that this was the moment we were in,

634
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,880
 but she's eight months pregnant.

635
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:08,200
 She has been with child for a long time,

636
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:11,760
 and yet her to-do list has not gotten any shorter.

637
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:13,280
 Neither has mine.

638
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:15,100
 Her to-do list has not gotten any shorter.

639
00:25:15,100 --> 00:25:17,240
 If anything, it has gotten longer.

640
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:18,080
 Why?

641
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:20,880
 Because she still sees all the untapped potential

642
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:22,720
 of our home, all of the things

643
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:24,240
 that can be brought to bear.

644
00:25:24,240 --> 00:25:26,480
 So there's things on there like hanging ceiling fans

645
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:29,260
 and building flower beds and working out our budget.

646
00:25:29,260 --> 00:25:31,960
 She has all of this stuff kind of still assembled,

647
00:25:31,960 --> 00:25:34,400
 even though no one would blame her for just taking a break.

648
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:35,720
 Like, you're kind of growing a baby, you know?

649
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:36,560
 Like, that's sufficient.

650
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:37,840
 Why don't you just hang out for a little bit?

651
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:40,240
 But she has all of these eyes

652
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:43,800
 for the untapped potential of our home.

653
00:25:44,800 --> 00:25:46,280
 She's a godly woman because of it.

654
00:25:46,280 --> 00:25:51,280
 She sees not only what is, she sees what should be.

655
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:53,600
 That's what a godly woman does.

656
00:25:53,600 --> 00:25:54,800
 She's resourceful.

657
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:58,040
 So let me ask you ladies, are you like this?

658
00:25:58,040 --> 00:26:01,360
 Like, is your world better because you're a part of it?

659
00:26:01,360 --> 00:26:02,900
 Like, when you enter into a room,

660
00:26:02,900 --> 00:26:06,500
 does the emotional temperature change because you arrive?

661
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:09,720
 Does it rise for the better, or does it fall

662
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:14,040
 because you stir about the coldness of a company?

663
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:16,720
 What happens when you enter into a conversation?

664
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:20,000
 Does it feel like the gossip just piles up?

665
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:22,480
 Do you feel like you extend wisdom into that moment

666
00:26:22,480 --> 00:26:24,680
 and you bring peaceful resolution?

667
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:28,720
 What happens whenever you find yourself around your family?

668
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:31,000
 Like, there's a lot of division and tension

669
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,360
 in families today.

670
00:26:32,360 --> 00:26:34,160
 Are you a peacemaker?

671
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:36,880
 Or do you actually sow division further?

672
00:26:36,880 --> 00:26:40,040
 What is your role within the world in which you walk?

673
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:42,580
 Godly women, they see potential

674
00:26:42,580 --> 00:26:44,160
 and they work to make it a reality.

675
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,160
 Do you do that?

676
00:26:45,160 --> 00:26:48,920
 Or are you just focused on what am I doing in my life?

677
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:49,840
 Let me just tell you.

678
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:51,880
 Godly women do not just concern themselves

679
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:54,480
 with what am I doing in my life.

680
00:26:54,480 --> 00:26:57,000
 They're concerned with what does God want to do

681
00:26:57,000 --> 00:27:00,240
 in their life because I'm a part of it.

682
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:01,860
 That's what a godly woman does.

683
00:27:01,860 --> 00:27:05,880
 She sees potential and she moves to make it practical,

684
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:07,560
 to bring it into reality.

685
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:08,600
 She's resourceful.

686
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:11,680
 The second thing is that she's inspired.

687
00:27:11,680 --> 00:27:12,520
 I love this one.

688
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:14,600
 Proverbs 31, 14 says,

689
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:16,080
 "She is like the ships of the merchant.

690
00:27:16,080 --> 00:27:18,200
 "She brings her food from afar.

691
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:21,520
 "In the ancient world, imported goods from merchant ships

692
00:27:21,520 --> 00:27:24,140
 "were exciting because they were exotic.

693
00:27:24,140 --> 00:27:27,320
 "It gave people exposure to new sounds and smells

694
00:27:27,320 --> 00:27:28,900
 "and tastes and sights.

695
00:27:28,900 --> 00:27:31,340
 "It was an injection of the extraordinary

696
00:27:31,340 --> 00:27:32,600
 "into the ordinary."

697
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:34,060
 That's what this woman is like.

698
00:27:34,060 --> 00:27:35,760
 That's what godly women do.

699
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:37,400
 They don't just do the bare minimum.

700
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:39,600
 They go above and beyond.

701
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:40,580
 Why?

702
00:27:40,580 --> 00:27:43,140
 Because it benefits the people around them.

703
00:27:43,140 --> 00:27:45,900
 Let me just lay it out to you like this.

704
00:27:45,900 --> 00:27:50,740
 If you were to go on a date and he took you to Luby's,

705
00:27:50,740 --> 00:27:55,320
 the chances are you're not going on a second date.

706
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:56,660
 Why?

707
00:27:56,660 --> 00:27:57,900
 Isn't it edible?

708
00:27:57,900 --> 00:28:01,860
 Yes, but it's not enjoyable.

709
00:28:01,860 --> 00:28:05,040
 There's nothing enjoyable about that experience.

710
00:28:05,040 --> 00:28:07,480
 You want him to do what Christ has done,

711
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:08,960
 to not just give you life,

712
00:28:08,960 --> 00:28:11,860
 but to give you life abundantly, right?

713
00:28:11,860 --> 00:28:13,840
 That's what this means.

714
00:28:13,840 --> 00:28:17,020
 That you ladies, you're called to be inspired.

715
00:28:17,020 --> 00:28:18,580
 When my wife and I, when we travel,

716
00:28:18,580 --> 00:28:21,860
 we care so much about where we stay and what we eat.

717
00:28:21,860 --> 00:28:23,620
 Like we want a good vibe.

718
00:28:23,620 --> 00:28:25,140
 We want the lights to be down low.

719
00:28:25,140 --> 00:28:26,940
 We want to have memorable conversations.

720
00:28:26,940 --> 00:28:29,140
 We want a little bit of music in the background.

721
00:28:29,140 --> 00:28:31,420
 Like we want that whole experience to be incredible.

722
00:28:31,420 --> 00:28:34,020
 I want to eat something that I can't make at home, you know?

723
00:28:34,020 --> 00:28:35,380
 That's what I'm looking for.

724
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:40,380
 I want a taste of the extraordinary in my ordinary.

725
00:28:40,380 --> 00:28:42,480
 That's what a godly woman does.

726
00:28:42,480 --> 00:28:43,620
 Now, let me be very clear.

727
00:28:43,620 --> 00:28:45,180
 It's not saying you got to be a master chef.

728
00:28:45,180 --> 00:28:46,860
 It's not saying you need to be an interior designer.

729
00:28:46,860 --> 00:28:48,360
 It's not saying you got to be a professional homemaker.

730
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:49,860
 That's not what this is saying.

731
00:28:49,860 --> 00:28:54,000
 I love that it says she brought her food from afar.

732
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,020
 I don't know what that means.

733
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:56,980
 I don't know if it meant that she like flew lobster in

734
00:28:56,980 --> 00:28:59,300
 from the coast of Maine and she's like breaking out

735
00:28:59,300 --> 00:29:00,540
 the surf and turf for the fam.

736
00:29:00,540 --> 00:29:02,740
 Or if she just door dashed something very cool

737
00:29:02,740 --> 00:29:04,020
 that she saw across town

738
00:29:04,020 --> 00:29:04,940
 that she wanted to bring in for the family.

739
00:29:04,940 --> 00:29:06,940
 I have no idea how she's working this out.

740
00:29:06,940 --> 00:29:10,300
 But what I do know is she's working it out.

741
00:29:10,300 --> 00:29:14,300
 She cares about caring about people.

742
00:29:14,300 --> 00:29:18,180
 That's it in one sentence.

743
00:29:18,180 --> 00:29:20,980
 She cares about caring about people.

744
00:29:20,980 --> 00:29:22,220
 She's inspired.

745
00:29:22,220 --> 00:29:25,660
 The third thing on this is she's self-sacrificing.

746
00:29:25,660 --> 00:29:27,060
 Proverbs 31, 15 says,

747
00:29:27,060 --> 00:29:29,180
 "She rises while it is yet night.

748
00:29:29,180 --> 00:29:30,920
 "She provides food for her household

749
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:32,780
 "and portions for her maidens."

750
00:29:32,780 --> 00:29:36,060
 Meaning she not only knows what needs to happen

751
00:29:36,060 --> 00:29:37,060
 and what it takes to get it done,

752
00:29:37,060 --> 00:29:41,140
 but she gets it before the sun to make it happen.

753
00:29:41,140 --> 00:29:42,540
 All throughout this passage,

754
00:29:42,540 --> 00:29:43,720
 if you could read it in the Hebrew,

755
00:29:43,720 --> 00:29:45,680
 what you would see over and over and over again

756
00:29:45,680 --> 00:29:47,140
 is you would see warfare imagery,

757
00:29:47,140 --> 00:29:48,940
 which just again feels strange.

758
00:29:48,940 --> 00:29:53,180
 But I love that the proverb is setting women up

759
00:29:53,180 --> 00:29:57,780
 as this warrior, as someone of valor and courage.

760
00:29:57,780 --> 00:29:59,540
 And what you read as you go through this

761
00:29:59,540 --> 00:30:02,700
 is that this warrior woman does so many different things.

762
00:30:02,700 --> 00:30:04,780
 It tells you that she's a warrior.

763
00:30:04,780 --> 00:30:05,620
 She's valiant.

764
00:30:05,620 --> 00:30:06,440
 She's strong.

765
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:07,280
 She plunders.

766
00:30:07,280 --> 00:30:08,100
 She ascends.

767
00:30:08,100 --> 00:30:09,260
 She stretches out a hand.

768
00:30:09,260 --> 00:30:10,300
 She is extolled.

769
00:30:10,300 --> 00:30:12,860
 She laughs like a victorious king.

770
00:30:12,860 --> 00:30:15,460
 But this verse contains probably my favorite example

771
00:30:15,460 --> 00:30:18,100
 because what it does is it uses the word food.

772
00:30:18,100 --> 00:30:22,100
 And hold on.

773
00:30:22,100 --> 00:30:23,940
 It uses the word food,

774
00:30:23,940 --> 00:30:26,980
 which is actually in the Hebrew interpreted as prey.

775
00:30:28,660 --> 00:30:33,180
 What this is saying is that she brings food to her family

776
00:30:33,180 --> 00:30:35,340
 in the sense that she's a hunter-gatherer.

777
00:30:35,340 --> 00:30:38,380
 Like she doesn't wait for it to come to her.

778
00:30:38,380 --> 00:30:40,020
 She gets up early in the morning

779
00:30:40,020 --> 00:30:43,100
 before the sun is even up and she goes out and she gets it.

780
00:30:43,100 --> 00:30:47,780
 Like she is on the prowl hunting to provide for her family.

781
00:30:47,780 --> 00:30:51,340
 She doesn't just roll out of bed begrudgingly

782
00:30:51,340 --> 00:30:54,500
 with only indifference about the day.

783
00:30:54,500 --> 00:30:58,600
 No, she rises up knowing that she has a day full of purpose

784
00:30:58,600 --> 00:30:59,700
 She's not a victim.

785
00:30:59,700 --> 00:31:04,180
 Again, victims, they're subject to someone else's decision,

786
00:31:04,180 --> 00:31:05,620
 to someone else's decision-making.

787
00:31:05,620 --> 00:31:07,740
 But this woman, she makes her own decisions.

788
00:31:07,740 --> 00:31:09,140
 She calls her own shots.

789
00:31:09,140 --> 00:31:10,540
 She makes her own moves.

790
00:31:10,540 --> 00:31:12,060
 But what I love about that

791
00:31:12,060 --> 00:31:14,260
 is she doesn't do it for herself alone.

792
00:31:14,260 --> 00:31:15,980
 She does it for the sake of her family.

793
00:31:15,980 --> 00:31:19,540
 She is not insecure with something to prove.

794
00:31:19,540 --> 00:31:22,180
 No, she is wildly secure.

795
00:31:22,180 --> 00:31:24,420
 And so she has something to offer.

796
00:31:24,420 --> 00:31:25,980
 You see how that works?

797
00:31:25,980 --> 00:31:27,820
 That's what's true of her.

798
00:31:27,820 --> 00:31:32,740
 We see that she was willing to sacrifice

799
00:31:32,740 --> 00:31:34,440
 so that others might succeed.

800
00:31:34,440 --> 00:31:38,820
 And then the fourth one on this is she's forward-thinking.

801
00:31:38,820 --> 00:31:40,420
 She's forward-thinking.

802
00:31:40,420 --> 00:31:43,880
 Verse 16 says, she considers a field and she buys it.

803
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:46,300
 With the fruit of her hands, she plants a vineyard.

804
00:31:46,300 --> 00:31:47,140
 I love this.

805
00:31:47,140 --> 00:31:48,780
 According to the proverb,

806
00:31:48,780 --> 00:31:53,780
 this woman, she has a husband, she has a family,

807
00:31:53,780 --> 00:31:56,900
 but she's still making big money moves.

808
00:31:56,900 --> 00:31:59,060
 You know, like she's not just laying back

809
00:31:59,060 --> 00:32:00,180
 and doing the trad wife thing.

810
00:32:00,180 --> 00:32:02,060
 Like she is totally leaning forward

811
00:32:02,060 --> 00:32:04,920
 and she's considering what's my business?

812
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:06,080
 Where are my investments?

813
00:32:06,080 --> 00:32:08,620
 How can I continue to make decisions in a way

814
00:32:08,620 --> 00:32:11,140
 that supports my family and uplifts the community?

815
00:32:11,140 --> 00:32:13,580
 Now, to be very clear, this is not saying

816
00:32:13,580 --> 00:32:16,460
 that staying at home moms are worse or lesser

817
00:32:16,460 --> 00:32:18,220
 than those moms that are out there working.

818
00:32:18,220 --> 00:32:21,220
 This is not making a commentary about that in the slightest.

819
00:32:21,220 --> 00:32:23,820
 For the record, both are full-time jobs.

820
00:32:25,220 --> 00:32:27,520
 So to be very clear, that's not what this is communicating.

821
00:32:27,520 --> 00:32:31,860
 But what it is communicating is that she is forward-thinking,

822
00:32:31,860 --> 00:32:35,300
 that she considers what she has, how well it's going,

823
00:32:35,300 --> 00:32:37,780
 and how she can leverage that to continue to further

824
00:32:37,780 --> 00:32:38,980
 what God is doing through her life

825
00:32:38,980 --> 00:32:40,740
 for the benefit of other people.

826
00:32:40,740 --> 00:32:42,180
 Here's the reason why we bring it up now,

827
00:32:42,180 --> 00:32:43,660
 because it's important for you,

828
00:32:43,660 --> 00:32:45,820
 if you're hearing you don't have a man yet.

829
00:32:45,820 --> 00:32:48,580
 Some of you ladies, you're waiting on a man

830
00:32:48,580 --> 00:32:51,300
 to begin living your life.

831
00:32:51,300 --> 00:32:55,620
 But godly women do not wait because Christ has already come.

832
00:32:55,620 --> 00:32:59,580
 They don't need him to show up because he's already done so.

833
00:32:59,580 --> 00:33:05,280
 So I'm just encouraging you to live forward-thinking,

834
00:33:05,280 --> 00:33:10,280
 meaning have eyes for the future that God wants you to find.

835
00:33:10,280 --> 00:33:13,420
 I remember when we lived in Houston,

836
00:33:13,420 --> 00:33:14,860
 I had a young lady approach me.

837
00:33:14,860 --> 00:33:16,660
 She was y'all's age, in her 20s and 30s,

838
00:33:16,660 --> 00:33:18,980
 and she came up and she worked in banking,

839
00:33:18,980 --> 00:33:20,100
 and what she really wanted to do

840
00:33:20,100 --> 00:33:23,260
 is she wanted to lead a class for all of her peers,

841
00:33:23,260 --> 00:33:25,420
 the other 20 and 30-something singles,

842
00:33:25,420 --> 00:33:30,180
 specifically women, around budgeting and financial acumen.

843
00:33:30,180 --> 00:33:31,420
 She was like, "I need to teach these girls

844
00:33:31,420 --> 00:33:32,380
 "how to do these things."

845
00:33:32,380 --> 00:33:34,060
 And I was like, "Why?

846
00:33:34,060 --> 00:33:36,760
 "That seems good, but walk me through the passion point,

847
00:33:36,760 --> 00:33:38,140
 "'cause you got a lot of energy for it."

848
00:33:38,140 --> 00:33:41,220
 And what she told me is that so many women

849
00:33:41,220 --> 00:33:42,440
 think that this is just gonna happen

850
00:33:42,440 --> 00:33:43,480
 whenever they get married.

851
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,620
 But the truth of the matter is,

852
00:33:44,620 --> 00:33:48,260
 marriage isn't promised, but your bills are promised.

853
00:33:48,260 --> 00:33:49,220
 They're coming.

854
00:33:49,220 --> 00:33:51,460
 And so you gotta know what to do with those things.

855
00:33:51,460 --> 00:33:54,280
 It's important that you don't wait for a man

856
00:33:54,280 --> 00:33:56,840
 to push forward into your life,

857
00:33:56,840 --> 00:33:59,220
 to figure out your finances, to purchase your own place,

858
00:33:59,220 --> 00:34:01,060
 to advance your career, to lead in your church,

859
00:34:01,060 --> 00:34:02,620
 to invest in other women.

860
00:34:02,620 --> 00:34:04,660
 You push forward because Christ,

861
00:34:04,660 --> 00:34:07,520
 he has a future for you to find, amen?

862
00:34:07,520 --> 00:34:11,580
 All right, let's keep going.

863
00:34:11,580 --> 00:34:13,160
 Next one's in 17 through 19.

864
00:34:13,160 --> 00:34:18,180
 A godly woman is strong.

865
00:34:18,180 --> 00:34:20,340
 A godly woman is strong.

866
00:34:20,340 --> 00:34:22,940
 And this one, it breaks down in two ways

867
00:34:22,940 --> 00:34:24,380
 if you wanna write these.

868
00:34:24,380 --> 00:34:28,100
 How does her strength actually demonstrate itself?

869
00:34:28,100 --> 00:34:30,100
 Number one is it demonstrates itself

870
00:34:30,100 --> 00:34:32,560
 in that she is persevering.

871
00:34:32,560 --> 00:34:33,400
 She's persevering.

872
00:34:33,400 --> 00:34:36,140
 Verse 17 says, "She dresses herself with strength

873
00:34:36,140 --> 00:34:39,260
 "and she makes her arms strong."

874
00:34:39,260 --> 00:34:43,060
 Literally, this is saying that she girds up her loins,

875
00:34:43,060 --> 00:34:45,500
 which feels kind of odd,

876
00:34:46,540 --> 00:34:48,340
 'cause many of us don't know what that means.

877
00:34:48,340 --> 00:34:50,180
 And yet, it's so interesting.

878
00:34:50,180 --> 00:34:54,900
 What this is saying is that she prepares herself

879
00:34:54,900 --> 00:34:57,740
 in her outward adornment for the battle at hand.

880
00:34:57,740 --> 00:35:00,800
 Whenever you would see warriors in the ancient Near East

881
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:02,860
 wearing robes into battle, they would gird up their loins,

882
00:35:02,860 --> 00:35:03,980
 meaning they would pull up their robe

883
00:35:03,980 --> 00:35:06,140
 and they would tuck it into their belt

884
00:35:06,140 --> 00:35:08,460
 so that way they could move, so that way they could run,

885
00:35:08,460 --> 00:35:09,660
 so that way they could fight.

886
00:35:09,660 --> 00:35:12,340
 She knows difficult days are ahead of me.

887
00:35:12,340 --> 00:35:13,940
 Trouble is on the horizon.

888
00:35:13,940 --> 00:35:17,180
 Temptation will come, I will get beat down,

889
00:35:17,180 --> 00:35:19,500
 so let me get myself ready.

890
00:35:19,500 --> 00:35:23,000
 Let me strengthen myself and adorn myself appropriately

891
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:25,140
 for the fight that is at hand.

892
00:35:25,140 --> 00:35:27,740
 She's not gullible, that's the assumption.

893
00:35:27,740 --> 00:35:30,980
 She knows the world is dark, evil abounds,

894
00:35:30,980 --> 00:35:34,600
 and temptation will come, so let me be ready for it.

895
00:35:34,600 --> 00:35:37,980
 It says that she makes her arms strong,

896
00:35:37,980 --> 00:35:43,260
 meaning they're not naturally that way.

897
00:35:43,260 --> 00:35:44,700
 Could mean she's on creatine,

898
00:35:44,700 --> 00:35:47,100
 probably means they're not naturally that way,

899
00:35:47,100 --> 00:35:51,020
 and so what she does is she knows everything that is ahead,

900
00:35:51,020 --> 00:35:52,500
 and yet when she does get knocked down,

901
00:35:52,500 --> 00:35:53,960
 when people do take advantage of her,

902
00:35:53,960 --> 00:35:58,020
 when she does find herself at the bottom of her barrel,

903
00:35:58,020 --> 00:36:00,540
 she will gird her loins, she will strengthen her arms,

904
00:36:00,540 --> 00:36:02,900
 and she will move forward.

905
00:36:02,900 --> 00:36:04,660
 I want my daughter to be like this,

906
00:36:04,660 --> 00:36:07,200
 full of humility and tenacity.

907
00:36:07,200 --> 00:36:10,340
 That's what I want for you.

908
00:36:10,340 --> 00:36:13,740
 I want your life to be full of grace

909
00:36:13,740 --> 00:36:15,040
 with a little crazy in there.

910
00:36:15,040 --> 00:36:18,500
 That's what should be true of a godly woman.

911
00:36:18,500 --> 00:36:20,820
 You see, modern society is trying to pit you

912
00:36:20,820 --> 00:36:21,700
 into one of two places.

913
00:36:21,700 --> 00:36:23,620
 It wants you to be a trad wife.

914
00:36:23,620 --> 00:36:25,740
 All humility, no tenacity.

915
00:36:25,740 --> 00:36:27,460
 You don't need a man, or you do need a man,

916
00:36:27,460 --> 00:36:29,500
 you exist to serve, you're gonna have to raise babies

917
00:36:29,500 --> 00:36:31,740
 for the rest of your life, that's your future.

918
00:36:31,740 --> 00:36:32,980
 The other side of the spectrum says

919
00:36:32,980 --> 00:36:34,500
 you should be a boss wife,

920
00:36:34,500 --> 00:36:36,120
 so all tenacity and no humility,

921
00:36:36,120 --> 00:36:37,300
 meaning you don't need anybody,

922
00:36:37,300 --> 00:36:38,400
 you can do everything yourself,

923
00:36:38,400 --> 00:36:39,660
 no one can tell you what to do,

924
00:36:39,660 --> 00:36:40,860
 but the truth of the matter is,

925
00:36:40,860 --> 00:36:43,660
 you cannot be either or, you must have both and.

926
00:36:43,660 --> 00:36:46,460
 You must have tenacity, you must have humility,

927
00:36:46,460 --> 00:36:47,980
 because then you can move through this world

928
00:36:47,980 --> 00:36:51,300
 in the way that God has called you to do so.

929
00:36:51,300 --> 00:36:53,140
 You're not a victim, you're a victor.

930
00:36:53,140 --> 00:36:56,620
 You should have respect for your limitations,

931
00:36:56,620 --> 00:37:00,620
 but you should have enough crazy to push the limits.

932
00:37:00,620 --> 00:37:06,540
 I want you to be confident without being arrogant.

933
00:37:08,580 --> 00:37:12,440
 I want you to be capable without being self-sufficient.

934
00:37:12,440 --> 00:37:18,300
 I want you to be industrious, but not merciless.

935
00:37:18,300 --> 00:37:21,580
 And I want you to be generous without being proud.

936
00:37:21,580 --> 00:37:23,740
 That's what this looks like.

937
00:37:23,740 --> 00:37:27,580
 I want that for you, and I want you to want it for yourself.

938
00:37:27,580 --> 00:37:30,100
 The second way that her strength manifests itself

939
00:37:30,100 --> 00:37:31,820
 is she's peaceable.

940
00:37:31,820 --> 00:37:36,820
 True strength is not just the willingness to fight,

941
00:37:36,860 --> 00:37:39,900
 but the ability to withhold oneself,

942
00:37:39,900 --> 00:37:42,140
 control oneself from the fight,

943
00:37:42,140 --> 00:37:43,940
 and that's what we see is true of her.

944
00:37:43,940 --> 00:37:44,940
 It says in verse 16,

945
00:37:44,940 --> 00:37:48,300
 she perceives that her merchandise is profitable.

946
00:37:48,300 --> 00:37:50,400
 Her lamp does not go out at night.

947
00:37:50,400 --> 00:37:53,400
 I'll be quick on this one, just for the sake of time,

948
00:37:53,400 --> 00:37:55,780
 but I think it's important you understand.

949
00:37:55,780 --> 00:37:57,380
 She's looking at her bank statement,

950
00:37:57,380 --> 00:38:00,620
 and she's realizing, I'm doing all right.

951
00:38:00,620 --> 00:38:01,740
 Like, I got some money in the bank.

952
00:38:01,740 --> 00:38:02,880
 Things are going well for me.

953
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:05,700
 She actually enjoys the fruit of her labor.

954
00:38:05,700 --> 00:38:10,420
 She embraces the peace that comes from her productivity.

955
00:38:10,420 --> 00:38:11,880
 Here's what's crazy.

956
00:38:11,880 --> 00:38:14,460
 We live in a world where it is either prosperity gospel

957
00:38:14,460 --> 00:38:16,060
 or it is poverty gospel,

958
00:38:16,060 --> 00:38:19,140
 where you should either expect that God will give you

959
00:38:19,140 --> 00:38:21,540
 everything you want, health, wealth, and fame.

960
00:38:21,540 --> 00:38:23,580
 It's yours, but that's not true.

961
00:38:23,580 --> 00:38:26,740
 Or we expect that we must only give, give, give, give,

962
00:38:26,740 --> 00:38:28,300
 give, give, give, give, give, give, give, give,

963
00:38:28,300 --> 00:38:30,740
 and deplete ourselves and never enjoy

964
00:38:30,740 --> 00:38:33,520
 the sort of abundant life that Christ came to give.

965
00:38:33,520 --> 00:38:35,060
 It's neither of those things.

966
00:38:35,060 --> 00:38:37,480
 The truth of the matter is, you're meant to be productive.

967
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:38,320
 We're gonna see later.

968
00:38:38,320 --> 00:38:40,780
 You're meant to provide, but as you do that,

969
00:38:40,780 --> 00:38:41,980
 you should experience peace,

970
00:38:41,980 --> 00:38:44,180
 the joy that comes with walking with God

971
00:38:44,180 --> 00:38:46,780
 and living the life He has destined you to do.

972
00:38:46,780 --> 00:38:48,820
 So what does this look like for you, ladies?

973
00:38:48,820 --> 00:38:51,420
 It's crazy that I'm actually doing this.

974
00:38:51,420 --> 00:38:53,580
 It looks like maybe you should take a trip.

975
00:38:53,580 --> 00:38:56,300
 Like, maybe, thank you, Trisha.

976
00:38:56,300 --> 00:38:58,820
 Like, maybe you should grab some friends,

977
00:38:58,820 --> 00:39:00,500
 and you should go, and you should check out a place

978
00:39:00,500 --> 00:39:01,340
 that you've wanted to visit.

979
00:39:01,340 --> 00:39:03,460
 Maybe you should book some time on the calendar

980
00:39:03,460 --> 00:39:05,580
 every quarter, and you should just get together,

981
00:39:05,580 --> 00:39:07,620
 and you should enjoy a dinner with one another.

982
00:39:07,620 --> 00:39:09,220
 Maybe it's buying those shoes if you've been to INI.

983
00:39:09,220 --> 00:39:10,040
 I don't know.

984
00:39:10,040 --> 00:39:11,740
 I'm not saying that you gotta make a habit of this,

985
00:39:11,740 --> 00:39:13,740
 but I am saying that you will learn

986
00:39:13,740 --> 00:39:15,380
 greater gratitude from God

987
00:39:15,380 --> 00:39:17,500
 by not just acknowledging His provision,

988
00:39:17,500 --> 00:39:20,740
 but by actually enjoying it.

989
00:39:20,740 --> 00:39:22,580
 Does that make sense?

990
00:39:22,580 --> 00:39:23,740
 It's not a license to get out there

991
00:39:23,740 --> 00:39:24,580
 and just do what you want.

992
00:39:24,580 --> 00:39:25,420
 That's not what I'm saying.

993
00:39:25,420 --> 00:39:28,100
 This is not a self-help gospel.

994
00:39:28,100 --> 00:39:32,320
 This is not license to therapeutize the scriptures.

995
00:39:32,320 --> 00:39:33,260
 That's not what I'm saying.

996
00:39:33,260 --> 00:39:35,900
 But what I am saying is this gives you the opportunity

997
00:39:35,900 --> 00:39:39,100
 to enjoy what God has come to give

998
00:39:39,100 --> 00:39:43,220
 because your merchandise is profitable.

999
00:39:43,220 --> 00:39:48,060
 Let's keep going.

1000
00:39:48,060 --> 00:39:52,920
 Verse 20 says, "She opens her hand to the poor,

1001
00:39:52,920 --> 00:39:54,660
 "and she reaches out her hand to the needy."

1002
00:39:54,660 --> 00:39:57,380
 This is the hinge of the entire section,

1003
00:39:57,380 --> 00:39:58,420
 because what this is telling us

1004
00:39:58,420 --> 00:40:00,860
 is that she's going from just producing in life

1005
00:40:00,860 --> 00:40:02,660
 to now providing for other people.

1006
00:40:02,660 --> 00:40:05,540
 We learn that a godly woman is compassionate.

1007
00:40:05,540 --> 00:40:08,060
 She's compassionate, meaning she's generous.

1008
00:40:08,060 --> 00:40:11,540
 Like the same hands that worked the distaff and the spindle,

1009
00:40:11,540 --> 00:40:13,380
 they're now open to the needy.

1010
00:40:13,380 --> 00:40:14,300
 I love the turn of that.

1011
00:40:14,300 --> 00:40:16,220
 Verses 19 to 20.

1012
00:40:16,220 --> 00:40:19,120
 And because she does this, this is important,

1013
00:40:19,120 --> 00:40:22,700
 she's able to take care of people that are around her,

1014
00:40:22,700 --> 00:40:24,580
 not just her own home,

1015
00:40:24,580 --> 00:40:26,260
 but for the sake of the community as well.

1016
00:40:26,260 --> 00:40:27,540
 I remember when we lived in Houston,

1017
00:40:27,540 --> 00:40:31,320
 there were a group of young single ladies in the ministry

1018
00:40:31,320 --> 00:40:34,180
 that they had befriended an exotic dancer,

1019
00:40:34,180 --> 00:40:35,980
 a girl that was coming through a worship gathering

1020
00:40:35,980 --> 00:40:37,780
 that we had similar to this, and they got to know her,

1021
00:40:37,780 --> 00:40:40,900
 and they realized, man, you're genuinely amazing,

1022
00:40:40,900 --> 00:40:42,060
 and we'd love to get to know the girls

1023
00:40:42,060 --> 00:40:42,900
 that are dancing with you.

1024
00:40:42,900 --> 00:40:45,780
 And so they started making weekly trips to the club.

1025
00:40:45,780 --> 00:40:47,780
 And what they did is they showed up, not at night,

1026
00:40:47,780 --> 00:40:49,420
 in the day, and they would drink Sprite,

1027
00:40:49,420 --> 00:40:50,700
 and they would just hang out with the girl,

1028
00:40:50,700 --> 00:40:51,820
 and they would get to know them.

1029
00:40:51,820 --> 00:40:54,420
 And they just wanted to extend the love of Jesus.

1030
00:40:54,420 --> 00:40:57,660
 And as they did this, girls came to know Christ.

1031
00:40:57,660 --> 00:40:59,840
 And girls ended up leaving that club.

1032
00:40:59,840 --> 00:41:01,820
 One bouncer ended up leaving that club.

1033
00:41:01,820 --> 00:41:06,420
 Like, they made haste towards where Christ himself was,

1034
00:41:06,420 --> 00:41:08,180
 and it was because these girls were generous

1035
00:41:08,180 --> 00:41:10,020
 with their time, they were generous with their money,

1036
00:41:10,020 --> 00:41:12,460
 they were generous with their energy.

1037
00:41:12,460 --> 00:41:15,940
 You see, there's a difference

1038
00:41:15,940 --> 00:41:17,840
 between a woman who's compassionate in theory

1039
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:20,740
 and a woman who is compassionate in practice.

1040
00:41:20,740 --> 00:41:22,820
 It is easy to feel bad about the world's problems

1041
00:41:22,820 --> 00:41:24,140
 from a safe distance.

1042
00:41:24,140 --> 00:41:26,740
 We're prolific at this.

1043
00:41:26,740 --> 00:41:29,340
 We repost, and we pray quick prayers,

1044
00:41:29,340 --> 00:41:31,380
 and we say, "That's so sad," and then we keep on scrolling.

1045
00:41:31,380 --> 00:41:33,620
 But a godly woman does not move on so quickly.

1046
00:41:33,620 --> 00:41:36,740
 She moves in very quickly.

1047
00:41:36,740 --> 00:41:38,800
 She moves towards the needs that she sees,

1048
00:41:38,800 --> 00:41:40,940
 and she seeks to resolve them.

1049
00:41:40,940 --> 00:41:43,400
 And then she's thoughtful, she's thoughtful.

1050
00:41:43,400 --> 00:41:45,840
 Verses 21 and 22 says,

1051
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:50,280
 "She is not afraid of snow for her household."

1052
00:41:50,280 --> 00:41:51,260
 Neither are we, you know,

1053
00:41:51,260 --> 00:41:53,140
 triple-digit heat out here in Texas.

1054
00:41:53,140 --> 00:41:56,580
 Snow would be nice, would take a little bit of that.

1055
00:41:56,580 --> 00:41:58,640
 "For all her household are clothed in scarlet.

1056
00:41:58,640 --> 00:42:00,500
 "She makes bed coverings for herself.

1057
00:42:00,500 --> 00:42:03,580
 "Her clothing is fine linen and in purple."

1058
00:42:03,580 --> 00:42:06,580
 What does it mean when she says she does not fear the snow?

1059
00:42:06,580 --> 00:42:10,520
 It's saying that she sees around corners,

1060
00:42:10,520 --> 00:42:11,680
 she anticipates needs,

1061
00:42:11,680 --> 00:42:15,020
 she is solving problems before problems arise.

1062
00:42:15,020 --> 00:42:17,940
 Like, she does so by way of making scarlet,

1063
00:42:17,940 --> 00:42:19,540
 which is ultimately thoughtful.

1064
00:42:19,540 --> 00:42:22,460
 Like, why is scarlet so significant in this moment?

1065
00:42:22,460 --> 00:42:24,540
 Because dark garments,

1066
00:42:24,540 --> 00:42:27,260
 you've been learning this by practice in Texas,

1067
00:42:27,260 --> 00:42:32,260
 dark garments absorb heat better than light garments.

1068
00:42:32,260 --> 00:42:34,540
 But not only do they absorb it, they retain it.

1069
00:42:34,540 --> 00:42:37,700
 So she is preparing a suitable kind of clothing

1070
00:42:37,700 --> 00:42:40,060
 for her family that will not only keep them warm,

1071
00:42:40,060 --> 00:42:41,620
 but will keep them warm.

1072
00:42:41,620 --> 00:42:44,940
 She's anticipating the needs.

1073
00:42:44,940 --> 00:42:46,340
 She understands her kids are gonna come

1074
00:42:46,340 --> 00:42:47,460
 and they're gonna say, "I'm cold."

1075
00:42:47,460 --> 00:42:50,420
 And she's gonna go, "I've got clothes for you."

1076
00:42:50,420 --> 00:42:52,020
 I don't want it to be ugly.

1077
00:42:52,020 --> 00:42:53,180
 Well, here it is, it's in scarlet.

1078
00:42:53,180 --> 00:42:57,340
 Like, she knows it could be black, which is functional,

1079
00:42:57,340 --> 00:42:59,820
 but I'll make it scarlet because it should be beautiful.

1080
00:42:59,820 --> 00:43:04,820
 She understands thoughtfulness matters in the eyes of God.

1081
00:43:04,820 --> 00:43:07,000
 Are you thoughtful like that?

1082
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:08,540
 Like, when you enter into a room, ladies,

1083
00:43:08,540 --> 00:43:09,880
 are you a stress amplifier?

1084
00:43:09,880 --> 00:43:11,900
 Are people like, "Oh my gosh, here she comes."

1085
00:43:11,900 --> 00:43:15,340
 Or are you a stress reducer?

1086
00:43:15,340 --> 00:43:17,180
 Do people breathe a sigh of relief

1087
00:43:17,180 --> 00:43:19,860
 because you've walked into the building?

1088
00:43:19,860 --> 00:43:21,180
 I remember at our wedding,

1089
00:43:21,180 --> 00:43:24,020
 one of my wife's dear high school friends looked at her,

1090
00:43:24,020 --> 00:43:26,440
 a longtime friend looked at her,

1091
00:43:26,440 --> 00:43:29,020
 and there were so many kind words said at our wedding.

1092
00:43:29,020 --> 00:43:31,420
 I don't know why I remember this,

1093
00:43:31,420 --> 00:43:33,680
 but this friend looked at her and she said,

1094
00:43:33,680 --> 00:43:35,260
 "Brooke is like home."

1095
00:43:35,260 --> 00:43:38,420
 And I remember thinking to myself,

1096
00:43:38,420 --> 00:43:43,100
 Brooke has anticipated the needs of this girl for so long.

1097
00:43:43,100 --> 00:43:46,140
 She has sought to solve the problems before they ever arise.

1098
00:43:46,140 --> 00:43:48,620
 She has provided safety for her.

1099
00:43:49,780 --> 00:43:51,500
 She has clothed her in scarlet.

1100
00:43:51,500 --> 00:43:56,900
 You can be home for somebody too.

1101
00:43:56,900 --> 00:43:58,380
 You can do this likewise.

1102
00:43:58,380 --> 00:43:59,460
 You can be thoughtful.

1103
00:43:59,460 --> 00:44:01,460
 The fifth thing that you gotta know

1104
00:44:01,460 --> 00:44:03,900
 is a godly woman is secure.

1105
00:44:03,900 --> 00:44:06,300
 I could keep my time going just so I can see it.

1106
00:44:06,300 --> 00:44:09,660
 Why is she secure?

1107
00:44:09,660 --> 00:44:13,100
 Two things, number one, she's got good taste in men.

1108
00:44:13,100 --> 00:44:17,260
 Verse 23 says, "Her husband is known in the gates

1109
00:44:17,260 --> 00:44:19,620
 "when he sits among the elders of the land."

1110
00:44:19,620 --> 00:44:20,980
 What is that talking about?

1111
00:44:20,980 --> 00:44:22,780
 Well, you gotta know something about the gates.

1112
00:44:22,780 --> 00:44:24,680
 The gates were not just the entrance to the city.

1113
00:44:24,680 --> 00:44:26,380
 They were sort of like the courthouse

1114
00:44:26,380 --> 00:44:29,020
 where the elders of the community would gather together

1115
00:44:29,020 --> 00:44:31,320
 and they would adjudicate different issues.

1116
00:44:31,320 --> 00:44:32,740
 It's where reputations were made

1117
00:44:32,740 --> 00:44:34,140
 and it's where matters were settled.

1118
00:44:34,140 --> 00:44:36,820
 And her man has a seat at that table.

1119
00:44:36,820 --> 00:44:38,180
 That's who her guy is.

1120
00:44:38,180 --> 00:44:40,300
 Now, here's something really important about this text.

1121
00:44:40,300 --> 00:44:43,500
 It is not saying that she made him that way.

1122
00:44:43,500 --> 00:44:46,820
 It is saying she found him that way.

1123
00:44:46,820 --> 00:44:50,300
 He already had a seat at the table.

1124
00:44:50,300 --> 00:44:53,940
 He had a good name and she had some good taste.

1125
00:44:53,940 --> 00:44:57,140
 How do you know if you have bad taste in men?

1126
00:44:57,140 --> 00:45:00,260
 If you always say all men are jerks,

1127
00:45:00,260 --> 00:45:03,140
 the chances are just the ones you date are.

1128
00:45:03,140 --> 00:45:06,380
 Because this woman found a good man.

1129
00:45:06,380 --> 00:45:09,240
 And I know some really good men in this room.

1130
00:45:09,240 --> 00:45:11,540
 Like, they're not just out there, they're in here.

1131
00:45:11,540 --> 00:45:12,500
 There are good men.

1132
00:45:12,500 --> 00:45:14,580
 Oh, the guys are like, yeah, that's my guy right there.

1133
00:45:14,580 --> 00:45:18,620
 Like, there are good men.

1134
00:45:18,620 --> 00:45:20,560
 She found one, you can find one.

1135
00:45:20,560 --> 00:45:23,460
 And here's the amazing thing that she does to him.

1136
00:45:23,460 --> 00:45:25,420
 She elevates his reputation further.

1137
00:45:25,420 --> 00:45:27,540
 He had a good name, she comes into the picture.

1138
00:45:27,540 --> 00:45:28,920
 Now he has a great name.

1139
00:45:28,920 --> 00:45:30,320
 That's what's true for him.

1140
00:45:30,320 --> 00:45:33,560
 And the reason why is she's not trying to diminish him

1141
00:45:33,560 --> 00:45:34,740
 to make herself feel good.

1142
00:45:34,740 --> 00:45:36,340
 She's not competing with him.

1143
00:45:36,340 --> 00:45:38,660
 She's not for fear of not being equal,

1144
00:45:38,660 --> 00:45:40,340
 trying to pull him down and pull herself up.

1145
00:45:40,340 --> 00:45:41,620
 She's not trying to keep score.

1146
00:45:41,620 --> 00:45:43,180
 She's not calling her mom and venting to him

1147
00:45:43,180 --> 00:45:45,160
 about everything he did wrong this weekend.

1148
00:45:45,160 --> 00:45:46,000
 Why?

1149
00:45:46,000 --> 00:45:49,120
 Because his name is her name.

1150
00:45:49,120 --> 00:45:53,740
 And if she diminishes his name, she diminishes her name.

1151
00:45:53,740 --> 00:45:55,460
 Why does this matter for you if you're here

1152
00:45:55,460 --> 00:45:57,980
 and you're not linked up, married to a man yet?

1153
00:45:57,980 --> 00:46:00,100
 Because if you're not, his name is not your name.

1154
00:46:00,100 --> 00:46:01,620
 Let that be very clear.

1155
00:46:01,620 --> 00:46:04,820
 And yet it matters because if you have found a godly man,

1156
00:46:04,820 --> 00:46:06,600
 and that is a massive assumption.

1157
00:46:06,600 --> 00:46:09,060
 Some of you, you've found a good man.

1158
00:46:09,060 --> 00:46:10,500
 You've not found a godly man.

1159
00:46:11,700 --> 00:46:14,100
 Anyone that is not a godly man is not a good man

1160
00:46:14,100 --> 00:46:19,660
 because anything good comes from the giver

1161
00:46:19,660 --> 00:46:21,660
 of that which is good, which is God.

1162
00:46:21,660 --> 00:46:23,760
 He is the giver of every good and perfect gift.

1163
00:46:23,760 --> 00:46:25,540
 You must know him, you must know God

1164
00:46:25,540 --> 00:46:27,020
 if you are going to be good.

1165
00:46:27,020 --> 00:46:29,340
 That is what is true by way of the scripture.

1166
00:46:29,340 --> 00:46:31,940
 You must have a godly man.

1167
00:46:31,940 --> 00:46:35,260
 And if you do have a godly man, then what you can know

1168
00:46:37,480 --> 00:46:42,140
 is that guarding his name will guard your name

1169
00:46:42,140 --> 00:46:45,100
 should that name ever actually become yours.

1170
00:46:45,100 --> 00:46:48,060
 Ladies, let me ask you here in final.

1171
00:46:48,060 --> 00:46:49,700
 Are you attracted to who he is

1172
00:46:49,700 --> 00:46:52,260
 or are you attracted to who you think he'll become?

1173
00:46:52,260 --> 00:46:54,140
 Because here's the truth.

1174
00:46:54,140 --> 00:46:56,900
 You do not date a resume, you date a person.

1175
00:46:56,900 --> 00:47:01,660
 You don't confuse potential with character.

1176
00:47:01,660 --> 00:47:06,660
 You want a man that has protected his name, not damaged it.

1177
00:47:06,700 --> 00:47:08,940
 If he has not protected his name,

1178
00:47:08,940 --> 00:47:10,940
 what do you think he'll do with yours?

1179
00:47:10,940 --> 00:47:14,100
 Please, for the love.

1180
00:47:14,100 --> 00:47:16,060
 (congregation laughing)

1181
00:47:16,060 --> 00:47:18,640
 It's my girls down here, they know.

1182
00:47:18,640 --> 00:47:22,720
 You need a good man, you need a godly one.

1183
00:47:22,720 --> 00:47:27,060
 So she has good taste in men and then she's assured.

1184
00:47:27,060 --> 00:47:30,100
 Verse 25 says, "Strength and dignity are her clothing."

1185
00:47:30,100 --> 00:47:33,060
 And she laughs at the times to come.

1186
00:47:33,060 --> 00:47:35,460
 She's not clothing herself

1187
00:47:35,460 --> 00:47:37,460
 in whatever Instagram is targeting you with.

1188
00:47:37,460 --> 00:47:38,980
 She is not clothing herself

1189
00:47:38,980 --> 00:47:41,380
 in whatever your For You page is recommending.

1190
00:47:41,380 --> 00:47:43,760
 She is adorning herself, as we talked about early on,

1191
00:47:43,760 --> 00:47:45,740
 with what is internal and not external.

1192
00:47:45,740 --> 00:47:47,840
 And ladies, that matters more than you know

1193
00:47:47,840 --> 00:47:49,060
 because here's the deal.

1194
00:47:49,060 --> 00:47:50,660
 Listen to me very closely.

1195
00:47:50,660 --> 00:47:52,860
 You will either be loved for who you are

1196
00:47:52,860 --> 00:47:55,740
 or you will be lusted after what people see.

1197
00:47:55,740 --> 00:48:01,660
 One of those is gonna last

1198
00:48:01,660 --> 00:48:05,340
 and the other one won't.

1199
00:48:05,980 --> 00:48:08,100
 (congregation laughing)

1200
00:48:08,100 --> 00:48:13,100
 Your identity must be propped up on the son of God.

1201
00:48:13,100 --> 00:48:17,540
 It cannot be propped up on your appearance.

1202
00:48:17,540 --> 00:48:20,460
 It cannot be propped up on your like count.

1203
00:48:20,460 --> 00:48:23,540
 It cannot be propped up on how many followers you have.

1204
00:48:23,540 --> 00:48:27,420
 It cannot be propped up on anything but the cross.

1205
00:48:27,420 --> 00:48:31,180
 You build your identity on him.

1206
00:48:31,180 --> 00:48:32,940
 That's why she can laugh at the future.

1207
00:48:32,940 --> 00:48:34,060
 Don't you love that?

1208
00:48:35,220 --> 00:48:37,540
 How odd that must sound to so many of us.

1209
00:48:37,540 --> 00:48:39,540
 How can she do it?

1210
00:48:39,540 --> 00:48:41,060
 Because she knows what's coming.

1211
00:48:41,060 --> 00:48:45,120
 No, she knows who has come.

1212
00:48:45,120 --> 00:48:47,820
 She isn't anxious about tomorrow

1213
00:48:47,820 --> 00:48:50,580
 because she's not performing for tomorrow.

1214
00:48:50,580 --> 00:48:51,740
 She's living for today.

1215
00:48:51,740 --> 00:48:53,660
 You do the same.

1216
00:48:53,660 --> 00:48:56,740
 And then the last one here

1217
00:48:56,740 --> 00:48:59,780
 is a godly woman is praiseworthy.

1218
00:48:59,780 --> 00:49:02,880
 A godly woman is praiseworthy.

1219
00:49:04,040 --> 00:49:06,780
 Verse 27 says she looks well to the ways of her household.

1220
00:49:06,780 --> 00:49:08,540
 She does not eat the bread of idleness.

1221
00:49:08,540 --> 00:49:10,580
 Her children rise up and they call her blessed.

1222
00:49:10,580 --> 00:49:13,100
 Her husband also and he praises her.

1223
00:49:13,100 --> 00:49:14,960
 She's admirable.

1224
00:49:14,960 --> 00:49:18,820
 I love it.

1225
00:49:18,820 --> 00:49:19,920
 Her own kids, like the people who see

1226
00:49:19,920 --> 00:49:21,460
 her very most unfiltered self,

1227
00:49:21,460 --> 00:49:23,000
 like they catch her before 6 a.m.,

1228
00:49:23,000 --> 00:49:25,100
 before she's had a cup of coffee,

1229
00:49:25,100 --> 00:49:26,600
 before she's fixed her hair,

1230
00:49:26,600 --> 00:49:29,180
 before she's made it into the rest of her day

1231
00:49:29,180 --> 00:49:30,900
 while she's in the middle of meltdown.

1232
00:49:30,900 --> 00:49:32,820
 They are the ones that rise up and call her blessed.

1233
00:49:32,820 --> 00:49:34,340
 They see her not at her best but at her worst

1234
00:49:34,340 --> 00:49:37,100
 and they're like the worst of you is better than the rest.

1235
00:49:37,100 --> 00:49:39,780
 It's not a stranger's compliment.

1236
00:49:39,780 --> 00:49:41,780
 It's not some dude that doesn't know her name.

1237
00:49:41,780 --> 00:49:43,980
 It's not the verdict of what people think of her page.

1238
00:49:43,980 --> 00:49:47,660
 It is the people that know her that praise her.

1239
00:49:47,660 --> 00:49:49,420
 Are you praiseworthy?

1240
00:49:49,420 --> 00:49:50,380
 Are you praiseworthy?

1241
00:49:50,380 --> 00:49:52,120
 Here's the thing.

1242
00:49:52,120 --> 00:49:53,540
 There's a big difference

1243
00:49:53,540 --> 00:49:57,380
 in chasing praise and chasing attention.

1244
00:49:57,380 --> 00:50:00,460
 And the difference between the two is

1245
00:50:00,460 --> 00:50:04,140
 you will only find praise by way of your godliness

1246
00:50:04,140 --> 00:50:07,580
 because only God is worthy of praise, amen?

1247
00:50:07,580 --> 00:50:11,580
 But you will find as much attention as you want

1248
00:50:11,580 --> 00:50:15,520
 because you can work however hard you want

1249
00:50:15,520 --> 00:50:18,240
 and find it in all degrees of measure.

1250
00:50:18,240 --> 00:50:19,780
 Are you attention seeking?

1251
00:50:19,780 --> 00:50:23,100
 Do you say things because they're true

1252
00:50:23,100 --> 00:50:25,660
 or do you say things because they'll get a reaction?

1253
00:50:27,260 --> 00:50:30,560
 Do you stir up drama because peace is boring?

1254
00:50:30,560 --> 00:50:32,940
 Do you indulge gossip because,

1255
00:50:32,940 --> 00:50:34,820
 well, that's way more interesting?

1256
00:50:34,820 --> 00:50:37,560
 Or do you try to speak wisdom?

1257
00:50:37,560 --> 00:50:41,220
 Does everybody always know that you're hurt?

1258
00:50:41,220 --> 00:50:45,580
 Or do they actually know that you've been healed?

1259
00:50:45,580 --> 00:50:46,940
 Do you subtly post things

1260
00:50:46,940 --> 00:50:49,100
 hoping that one specific person sees them?

1261
00:50:49,100 --> 00:50:50,660
 I don't know what the case may be,

1262
00:50:50,660 --> 00:50:53,300
 but what I do know is that there's a big difference

1263
00:50:53,300 --> 00:50:54,820
 in chasing praise and chasing attention.

1264
00:50:54,820 --> 00:50:56,180
 And if you'll entrust yourself to Christ

1265
00:50:56,180 --> 00:50:58,500
 that you will find the praise that is worthy of him

1266
00:50:58,500 --> 00:50:59,760
 and lavished upon you.

1267
00:50:59,760 --> 00:51:07,980
 Proverbs 31, 29 says many women have done excellently

1268
00:51:07,980 --> 00:51:10,100
 but you, you surpassed them all.

1269
00:51:10,100 --> 00:51:11,900
 This is the word of a man that has looked upon her

1270
00:51:11,900 --> 00:51:13,820
 and said it's not just that you're fine,

1271
00:51:13,820 --> 00:51:15,700
 it's not just that you're okay,

1272
00:51:15,700 --> 00:51:16,580
 it's not just that there might be

1273
00:51:16,580 --> 00:51:17,620
 a better option along the way,

1274
00:51:17,620 --> 00:51:19,060
 it's a man that is looking upon her and saying,

1275
00:51:19,060 --> 00:51:20,220
 no, I have surveyed it all

1276
00:51:20,220 --> 00:51:22,780
 and I know there's no one quite like you.

1277
00:51:22,780 --> 00:51:24,900
 You have surpassed everyone.

1278
00:51:27,180 --> 00:51:30,260
 That's the kind of praise that's worthy of chasing,

1279
00:51:30,260 --> 00:51:33,020
 not an algorithm, not some guy.

1280
00:51:33,020 --> 00:51:36,220
 It's the praise of the people who know you and love you

1281
00:51:36,220 --> 00:51:39,060
 because they know God and they love God.

1282
00:51:39,060 --> 00:51:40,640
 Let me finish by saying this.

1283
00:51:40,640 --> 00:51:42,980
 I have spent a lot of time

1284
00:51:42,980 --> 00:51:45,180
 considering my little girl who's on the way.

1285
00:51:45,180 --> 00:51:46,660
 She'll be here soon.

1286
00:51:46,660 --> 00:51:49,460
 And I cannot wait to introduce her to you all.

1287
00:51:49,460 --> 00:51:50,740
 She's gonna be the best.

1288
00:51:50,740 --> 00:51:55,640
 I have no idea how to help her become a woman.

1289
00:51:57,100 --> 00:52:01,340
 But God does.

1290
00:52:01,340 --> 00:52:04,740
 He knows what she needs, He knows what you need.

1291
00:52:04,740 --> 00:52:07,460
 And what we know by the end of this text

1292
00:52:07,460 --> 00:52:10,380
 is that you need fear the Lord.

1293
00:52:10,380 --> 00:52:13,060
 Charm is deceitful, beauty is vain.

1294
00:52:13,060 --> 00:52:16,140
 A woman who fears the Lord, she is the one to be praised.

1295
00:52:16,140 --> 00:52:17,380
 Give her the fruit of her hands,

1296
00:52:17,380 --> 00:52:19,420
 let her works praise her in the gates.

1297
00:52:19,420 --> 00:52:23,100
 Because you become God's woman

1298
00:52:24,220 --> 00:52:26,820
 by realizing Christ became your king.

1299
00:52:26,820 --> 00:52:28,260
 That's how this works.

1300
00:52:28,260 --> 00:52:29,840
 He's done all of this and more.

1301
00:52:29,840 --> 00:52:31,660
 He was trustworthy when we were faithless.

1302
00:52:31,660 --> 00:52:33,820
 He made the difference when we couldn't make it ourselves.

1303
00:52:33,820 --> 00:52:35,580
 He was strong when we were weak.

1304
00:52:35,580 --> 00:52:37,900
 He is compassionate when we don't deserve it.

1305
00:52:37,900 --> 00:52:40,580
 He is secure enough to walk even to the cross.

1306
00:52:40,580 --> 00:52:42,280
 And he is praiseworthy enough to know

1307
00:52:42,280 --> 00:52:45,500
 that God has given him the name that is above every name.

1308
00:52:45,500 --> 00:52:49,180
 Womanhood is not a goal to achieve, sisters.

1309
00:52:49,180 --> 00:52:51,180
 It is a gift of God to receive.

1310
00:52:51,180 --> 00:52:53,420
 He's extending it to you tonight.

1311
00:52:53,420 --> 00:52:54,420
 Will you reach out?

1312
00:52:54,420 --> 00:52:55,340
 Will you take it?

1313
00:52:55,340 --> 00:52:56,420
 Will you become it?

1314
00:52:56,420 --> 00:52:58,660
 Not over the course of a single evening,

1315
00:52:58,660 --> 00:53:00,380
 not over the course of this next week,

1316
00:53:00,380 --> 00:53:04,180
 but over the course of your life long as you walk with him.

1317
00:53:04,180 --> 00:53:06,620
 With eyes fixed on who he is,

1318
00:53:06,620 --> 00:53:11,380
 he will set your eyes to show you who you are too.

1319
00:53:11,380 --> 00:53:13,260
 And we pray that you would.

1320
00:53:13,260 --> 00:53:15,580
 God, I'm so thankful for this night,

1321
00:53:15,580 --> 00:53:17,780
 for this text, for these people,

1322
00:53:17,780 --> 00:53:20,020
 and for just the sufficiency of who you are.

1323
00:53:20,020 --> 00:53:21,780
 I'm grateful that God in a room like this,

1324
00:53:21,780 --> 00:53:24,100
 we can laugh together, and God, in this moment,

1325
00:53:24,100 --> 00:53:26,380
 we can cry together, and in the next moment,

1326
00:53:26,380 --> 00:53:27,500
 we can sing together.

1327
00:53:27,500 --> 00:53:28,660
 And God, over the course of an evening,

1328
00:53:28,660 --> 00:53:30,780
 we can experience the full range of emotion

1329
00:53:30,780 --> 00:53:32,920
 from rejoicing to repentance,

1330
00:53:32,920 --> 00:53:36,180
 because God, we know you're worthy of it all.

1331
00:53:36,180 --> 00:53:38,540
 And so Lord, now, as we do come into response,

1332
00:53:38,540 --> 00:53:40,580
 we want to respond.

1333
00:53:40,580 --> 00:53:42,780
 That's what happens in this moment.

1334
00:53:42,780 --> 00:53:46,820
 We recognize who you are, and we respond, oh God.

1335
00:53:46,820 --> 00:53:49,040
 Won't we respond accordingly?

1336
00:53:49,040 --> 00:53:51,340
 Won't you respond accordingly, my friends,

1337
00:53:51,340 --> 00:53:54,180
 my brothers, my sisters, gentlemen,

1338
00:53:54,180 --> 00:53:56,700
 your response is one where you have heard

1339
00:53:56,700 --> 00:53:57,900
 of the Proverbs 31 woman,

1340
00:53:57,900 --> 00:54:00,140
 and now you must search after her

1341
00:54:00,140 --> 00:54:02,500
 as she is more precious than jewels.

1342
00:54:02,500 --> 00:54:06,100
 To you sisters, you must respond by seeing,

1343
00:54:06,100 --> 00:54:07,820
 not a checklist of things to do,

1344
00:54:07,820 --> 00:54:10,680
 not a measuring stick to hold yourself up against,

1345
00:54:10,680 --> 00:54:13,220
 but a portrait of who God wishes you to become,

1346
00:54:13,220 --> 00:54:15,100
 and who he can fashion you in tonight.

1347
00:54:15,100 --> 00:54:16,820
 But the way that all this happens

1348
00:54:16,820 --> 00:54:19,720
 is not by waiting for it to take place in the future,

1349
00:54:19,720 --> 00:54:21,800
 but by taking a step right now.

1350
00:54:21,800 --> 00:54:25,620
 God, help us to do that in faith.

1351
00:54:25,620 --> 00:54:28,060
 Help us, God, to respond to you

1352
00:54:28,060 --> 00:54:30,260
 because you're worthy of responding too.

1353
00:54:30,260 --> 00:54:32,340
 Not God, because we want to be performative.

1354
00:54:32,340 --> 00:54:34,920
 Not God, because we're just trying to produce something.

1355
00:54:34,920 --> 00:54:37,060
 Not God, because we want to fit in with the rest,

1356
00:54:37,060 --> 00:54:40,160
 but because God, we just want to seek after you,

1357
00:54:40,160 --> 00:54:44,300
 for when we seek you, we will, God, be found by you.

1358
00:54:44,300 --> 00:54:46,380
 Help us to do that here in this moment.

1359
00:54:46,380 --> 00:54:47,880
 Help us, God, to respond.

1360
00:54:49,420 --> 00:54:53,340
 We love you, it's in Christ's name we pray, amen.

1361
00:54:53,340 --> 00:54:57,260
 Team is down to my right, team is down to my left,

1362
00:54:57,260 --> 00:54:59,740
 altar is open, space is yours.

1363
00:54:59,740 --> 00:55:01,980
 Don't rush out for the God

1364
00:55:01,980 --> 00:55:03,880
 who has waited for this night for you.

